Part 2: Derived code and assets (not MIT)
-----------------------------------------

Applies to everything not listed in Part 1, including:

  - WireView2/ (the desktop application), including its firmware images
    (WireView2/Firmware/) and background artwork (WireView2/Assets/Backgrounds/)
  - WireViewDeviceLib/
  - WireViewNet/Services/AppSettings.cs and WireViewNet/Services/XdgAutostart.cs
  - themes/

This code is derived from the original WireView Pro II Windows application by
Thermal Grizzly and from WireViewDeviceLib
(https://github.com/ElmorLabs-ThermalGrizzly/WireViewDeviceLib). Neither is
published under an open-source license, and the rights of the original authors
are reserved. The Linux-specific changes in these files are copyright (c) 2026
Emanuele Sparvoli.

These files are provided for personal use and for interoperability with
WireView Pro II hardware on Linux. No license to the original authors' code,
firmware or artwork is granted by this repository.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Thermal
Grizzly or ElmorLabs. WireView and Thermal Grizzly are trademarks of their
respective owners.


